        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57526fa3-e9fe-56bd-b399-1cc2b6ce629e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lucy Maud Montgomery, Jan Karon, Toby Tarnow\n- Works: Anne of Green Gables, Anne of Avonlea, Anne of Avonlea (1975 film)\n- Places: Canada\n- Topics: authorship, adaptations, portrayal of Anne Shirley\n\nFacts:\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was a Canadian author who lived from November 30, 1874 to April 24, 1942.\n- In 1908, Lucy Maud Montgomery began a novel series with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery published under the name L.M. Montgomery.\n- Toby Tarnow was the first actress to portray Anne Shirley of Anne of Green Gables on Canadian radio and later in a 1956 Canadian television movie.\n- Anne of Avonlea is the sequel to Anne of Green Gables by Lucy Maud Montgomery.\n- The 1975 film Anne of Avonlea is based on Anne of Avonlea.\n- Jan Karon is an American novelist who writes for both adults and young readers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
